{"name":"Blue Rodeo","hex":"#377d95","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"rodeo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A gathering of cattle to be branded.","A North American sport involving skills with horses, cows and other livestock."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To perform in a rodeo show."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rodeo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue Rodeo","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Rodeo is a Canadian rock band formed in 1984 in Toronto, Ontario. They have released 16 full-length studio albums, four live recordings, one greatest hits album, and two video/DVDs, along with multiple solo albums, side projects, and collaborations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Blue_Rodeo_%2853972453492%29.jpg/330px-Blue_Rodeo_%2853972453492%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Rodeo"},{"title":"Blue Rodeo (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Rodeo is a made for television drama film adapted from the novel of the same name by Jo-Ann Mapson. It first aired on CBS on October 20, 1996. Blue Rodeo was directed by Peter Werner and stars globally recognized artists, Ann-Margret and Kris Kristofferson."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/73/Blue_Rodeo_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Rodeo_(film)"},{"title":"Rodeo","blocks":[{"text":"Rodeo is a competitive equestrian sport that arose out of the working practices of cattle herding in Spain and Mexico, expanding throughout the Americas and to other nations. It was originally based on the skills required of the working vaqueros and, later, cowboys in what today is the western United States, western Canada, and northern Mexico. Today, it is a sporting event that involves horses and other livestock, designed to test the skill and speed of the cowboys and cowgirls.\nProfessional rodeos generally comprise the following events: tie-down roping, team roping, steer wrestling, saddle bronc riding, bareback bronc riding, bull riding, breakaway roping, and barrel racing. The events are divided into two basic categories: the timed events and rough stock events. Depending on sanctioning organization and region, other events such as goat tying and pole bending may also be a part of some rodeos. The \"world's first public cowboy contest\" was held on July 4, 1883, in Pecos, Texas, between cattle driver Trav Windham and roper Morg Livingston."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/StampedeRodeo2002.JPG/330px-StampedeRodeo2002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rodeo"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Blue_Rodeo_at_Slush_Puppie_Place_%2811.20.25%29.jpg/500px-Blue_Rodeo_at_Slush_Puppie_Place_%2811.20.25%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Blue_Rodeo_at_Slush_Puppie_Place_%2811.20.25%29.jpg/1280px-Blue_Rodeo_at_Slush_Puppie_Place_%2811.20.25%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Blue_Rodeo_at_Slush_Puppie_Place_%2811.20.25%29.jpg/500px-Blue_Rodeo_at_Slush_Puppie_Place_%2811.20.25%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blue Rodeo performs at Slush Puppie Place in Kingston, Ontario on November 20th, 2025","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_Rodeo_at_Slush_Puppie_Place_(11.20.25).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Cattle_branding_%28Grabill_1888%29.jpg/500px-Cattle_branding_%28Grabill_1888%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Cattle_branding_%28Grabill_1888%29.jpg/1280px-Cattle_branding_%28Grabill_1888%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Cattle_branding_%28Grabill_1888%29.jpg/500px-Cattle_branding_%28Grabill_1888%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Branding calves, 1888","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACattle_branding_(Grabill_1888).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0f/Buffalo_Bill%E2%80%99s_Mexican_Vaqueros_Riding_Wild_Cattle.jp